# [% site_name %]

> [% site_name %] documentation and site pages.

## Pages

[% FOREACH page IN pages %]
[%- # SM299: the source file's URL, which is NOT always the page URL plus ".md".
    # An index page's URL already ends in a slash, so appending ".md" produced
    # "<dir>/.md" - not a file. The homepage is an index page, so this was the
    # FIRST entry of every site's llms.txt, and the one an AI client is most
    # likely to follow.
    #
    # page.path looks like an easier answer and is wrong: it is docroot-relative,
    # so on a content-rooted domain it carries the sites/<name>/ prefix, which is
    # part of no public URL.
    src = page.url.search('/$') ? page.url _ 'index.md' : page.url _ '.md' -%]
- [[% page.title %]]([% site_url %][% src %])[% IF page.meta_desc %]: [% page.meta_desc %][% END %]
[% END %]
